Vikram and Betal: The Smart Rabbit

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a forest where all the animals lived in fear of a cruel lion,” said Betal. “The lion hunted them every day.”

The animals decided to send one animal each day to the lion so the others could live.

One day, it was a small rabbit’s turn.

The rabbit thought of a clever plan.

He reached the lion very late.

The lion became angry and said, “Why are you so late?”

The rabbit said, “Another lion tried to stop me and said he is the real king.”

The lion roared, “Take me to him!”

The rabbit took the lion to a deep well.

The lion looked inside and saw his own reflection.

Thinking it was another lion, he jumped into the well.

The rabbit escaped safely.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, how did the rabbit defeat the lion?”

Vikram replied, “By using intelligence instead of strength.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Intelligence is stronger than power.
